cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Injectivity of an Exponential Tent Transform"
abstract: >-
  Proofs and reproducible numerical checks for the uniqueness of the inverse
  problem for the exponential tent transform T(g)(x) = integral over t > 0 of
  exp(-integral_0^t integral_{x-tau}^{x+tau} g), the mean transformation time in
  the one-dimensional Kolmogorov-Johnson-Mehl-Avrami model. Equal transforms of
  two nonnegative locally integrable densities force equality whenever their
  difference has uniformly bounded mass on unit intervals; in particular the
  transform is injective on nonnegative L^p densities for every 1 <= p <= infinity,
  including infinite-mass L^2 densities. The release also includes an exact
  second-order identity, local information read from the transform, a
  controlled-tail injectivity theorem, and periodic local inversion, stability,
  regularity and reconstruction results. No closed-form inverse or
  literature-priority claim is made.
